💡 **SUGGESTION: the rewrite notice is prepended before tail-truncation, so long outputs silently drop it**

```dart
if (rewriteNotice != null) rawOutput = '$rewriteNotice\n$rawOutput';
final truncation = _truncateTail(rawOutput);
```

`_truncateTail` keeps the **tail**, so exactly when output is long enough to
truncate, the notice line at the head is cut and AC3's "the agent sees the
rewrite instead of discovering corruption by failure" silently doesn't happen on
the yield-inline path. The foreground path gets this right (the notice rides
`notices`/`_retryNoticePrefix`, which is prepended *after* truncation). Prepend
the notice after `_truncateTail` here too:

```dart
final truncation = _truncateTail(rawOutput);
final output = ...;
if (rewriteNotice != null) output = '$rewriteNotice\n$output';
```

